    "body": "# Problem:\r\nCurrently the only `root_marker` for Mojo is '.git' but not all Mojo projects are guaranteed to exist at the same level as a '.git' directory. [Even Modular's own repo containing the open-source code for the Mojo language](https://github.com/modular/modular) has a '.git' directory that is one-level above their Mojo folder.\r\n\r\n# Solution:\r\nPrefer 'pixi.toml' and 'pixi.lock' root_markers before '.git'. Modular recommends developers use the [Pixi package manager](https://pixi.prefix.dev) which is an alternative to `pip install` and Python virtual environments, and which creates `pixi.toml` and `pixi.lock` files at the root directory of your virtual environment. Proof of their recommendation can be found in two places:\r\n1. Step 1 of their [getting started doc](https://mojolang.org/docs/manual/get-started/) says \"we recommend using `pixi`\"\r\n<img width=\"668\" height=\"177\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/db71ac4b-3f98-4219-988a-71c6ccef93ea\" />\r\n\r\n2. Modular's repo containing the open-source code for Mojo has [\"pixi.toml\" and \"pixi.lock\" files at the root of their \"Mojo\" directory](https://github.com/modular/modular/tree/main/Mojo)",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-17T11:43:44Z",
